%% alt: User input and untrusted content such as retrieved documents, tool results and emails pass through input guardrails: first rules for size, format and allow and deny lists, then classifiers for harmful content, prompt attacks, personal data and topic. Input that passes goes to the model; input with personal data is masked first; blocked or flagged input gets a safe response and goes to a review queue and the log.
flowchart TB
  U[User input]:::human --> L
  D[Retrieved documents,<br/>tool results, emails]:::untrusted --> L
  subgraph C1[Input guardrails]
    L[Rules: size, format,<br/>allow and deny lists]:::control --> K[Classifiers: harmful content,<br/>prompt attacks, PII, topic]:::control
  end
  K -->|pass| M[Model]:::model
  K -->|mask| R[Redacted input]:::data --> M
  K -->|block or flag| H[Safe response,<br/>review queue, log]:::tool
